  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As has $968M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 126 awards with an average award size of $7.7M. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As obligations are up 14.3% year over year. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As received the full FY2026 to date amount from the Department of Defense, with a smaller buyer presence from the Department of the Interior at $72.5K. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As work is concentrated in guided missile and propulsion markets: Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing accounts for $576M, Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $222M, and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing accounts for $111M. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As also has obligations in Small Arms, Ordnance, and Ordnance Accessories Manufacturing at $35.3M and several smaller NAICS categories. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why is the FY2026 to date total at $968M?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $968M to Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As in FY2026 to date. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As obligations are up 14.3% year over year, reflecting larger award activity this fiscal year compared with prior years. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As averaged $7.7M per award across 126 awards, which pushed the total obligation to the current level."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As obligations concentrated?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing is the largest market for Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As at $576M. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is next at $222M, followed by Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $111M. Kongsberg Defence and Aerospace As also has obligations in Small Arms, Ordnance, and Ordnance Accessories Manufacturing at $35.3M and several smaller NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
  },
